\section*{Overview}
PROJECT G.A.L.A.C.T.I.C. is a multi-layer gravitational anomaly detection
and antigravity coupling stability engine. It integrates astrophysical
tensor fields, Hamiltonian dynamics, structural tensegrity analysis, and
timeline-based regime classification.

This README provides the laboratory-ready specification for installation,
execution, and interpretation of simulation results.

\section*{System Architecture}
The system is divided into four operational layers:

\subsection*{Layer 1: Astrophysical Intake}
Inputs:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Stellar kinematics (GAIA-like)
    \item CMB anisotropy tensor fields
    \item Quasar drift time-series
    \item Cosmic ray flux
\end{itemize}

Outputs:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Validated tensor field $T_{\mu\nu}(x)$
    \item Initial particle states $r_i(0), p_i(0)$
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Layer 2: Hamiltonian Dynamics Core}
Hamiltonian:
\[
H = \sum_i \left( \frac{p_i^2}{2m_i} + V(r_i) \right)
+ \sum_{i < j} \frac{G m_i m_j}{r_{ij}}
+ \Lambda \sum_i r_i^2
\]

Evolution:
\[
\dot{r}_i = \frac{p_i}{m_i}, \qquad
\dot{p}_i = -\frac{\partial H}{\partial r_i}
\]

Coupling constants:
\[
\alpha = \frac{1}{4\pi \epsilon_0}, \quad
\beta = \frac{G}{c^4}, \quad
\gamma = \frac{1}{2\omega_0^2}
\]

\subsection*{Layer 3: Structural Geometry \& Tensegrity}
Stress functional:
\[
S_{\text{geom}} = \sum_{(i,j)} k_{ij}^2 (r_{ij} - L_{ij})^2
\]

Outputs:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Stress magnitude
    \item Stress derivative
    \item Structural integrity score
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Layer 4: Event-Drift Timeline}
Regime classification:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Warped}: unstable curvature + rising stress
    \item \textbf{Stable}: bounded stress + consistent dynamics
    \item \textbf{Accelerating}: monotonic increase in anomaly strength
\end{itemize}

\section*{Simulation Requirements}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Python 3.11+
    \item NumPy, SciPy
    \item Optional: JAX or PyTorch for tensor acceleration
    \item Minimum RAM: 32 GB
\end{itemize}

\section*{Execution Workflow}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Load tensor field and initialize particle states.
    \item Define tensegrity structure and coupling parameters.
    \item Run Hamiltonian integration using a symplectic method.
    \item Compute structural stress each timestep.
    \item Classify regime every $N$ steps.
    \item Export trajectory, stress curve, and regime timeline.
\end{enumerate}

\section*{Outputs}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Trajectories $r_i(t), p_i(t)$
    \item Stress integrity curve $S_{\text{geom}}(t)$
    \item Regime timeline
    \item Parameter stability map
\end{itemize}

